course: dictionary
lesson: 15389
title: Guessing and checking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To speculate means to make a guess, or form an idea, about something when you do not have all the facts yet. A good guess has a reason behind it, but it is not yet a sure answer.
explain: «The sky is dark and the wind is cold, so I speculate that it will rain soon.» You cannot be sure yet, so you speculate. Then you check: look out of the window, or read the weather forecast.
explain: Speculate has a second meaning, about money. People speculate when they buy shares, land or currencies, hoping to sell them later for more. It is risky, because they could lose their money.
fact: Speculate is a verb: speculate, speculates, speculated, speculating.
fact: «Speculate» means to guess or form ideas when you do not have all the facts.
fact: In money, «speculate» means buying things like shares or land, hoping to sell them later for more, with a risk of losing money.
fact: Scientists and historians speculate, but then they look for evidence to check their guesses.
fact: A guess becomes useful when you test it.
exercise: «Nobody knows yet why the school bell rang early, so the class began to speculate.» What does speculate mean here? | Sing a song | *Guess about the reason | Go home | Copy the answer from the board
exercise: Which one shows someone speculating? | *They wonder why the lamp went out, and guess it was the wind | They read the map and walked to the lake | They counted all twenty coins twice | They wrote down the answer from the book
exercise: Dev says speculating about shares is safe money. What does speculate mean in money? | Save coins in a piggy bank safely | Give money to charity | Count coins in a jar | *Buy shares or land hoping to sell later for more, with a risk of losing money
test: Ms Patel says, «Don't just speculate, check.» What should you do? | Shout your guess loudly | Believe your guess is a fact | Stop thinking about it | *Look for evidence to see if your guess is right
test: Which form shows the action happening now? | speculate | speculated | *speculating
exam: Dad says people speculate about who will win the election on the news. What does speculate mean here? | Count all the votes carefully | Read the news aloud | *Make guesses without all the facts | Win the election
